+## Step 2.5 — Validate before building (gate)
+
+Run this before Step 3. It decides whether the extraction is good enough to send. On a healthy
+run it passes silently and nothing downstream changes.
+
+**Count `'N/A'`, not zeros.** A zero is usually a real value — `achievedToday` is legitimately
+`'0'` before the first sale of the day, and an empty task list is a real state. `'N/A'` is
+different: it only appears when a regex matched nothing, which means the page did not load, the
+session was not authenticated, or the markup moved.
+
+```javascript
+// Run against the assembled reportData, before generating the DOCX.
+const d = reportData.dashboardStats || {};
+const naCount = Object.values(d).filter(v => v === 'N/A').length;
+const fields  = Object.keys(d).length;
+
+const failures = [];
+if (reportData.loginOk === false)              failures.push('login did not reach My Dashboard');
+if (fields && naCount >= Math.ceil(fields * 0.6)) failures.push(`dashboard: ${naCount}/${fields} fields N/A`);
+if ((reportData.ytdLeaderboard || []).length === 0) failures.push('YTD leaderboard empty');
+if ((reportData.dailySales || []).length === 0)     failures.push('daily sales empty');
+
+failures;
+```
+
+**If `failures` is empty** — continue to Step 3 unchanged.
+
+**If `failures` is non-empty** — do **not** build the DOCX and do **not** send the briefing.
+A briefing full of `N/A` reads as a quiet day, not as a broken run, and that is the failure this
+gate exists to prevent. Instead send a plain-text email to the usual recipients:
+
+> Subject: `AZ briefing did not run — {date}`
+>
+> Body: the `failures` list, plus the URL of the first section that failed, so the run can be
+> repeated by hand.
+
+Then stop. Do not partially send, and do not substitute values from a previous day.
+
+---
